WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Temperatures above 30 degrees Celsius, a Pacific first, lock-in and unprecedented El Nino for the world. This is Omni View Top World News, episode 21. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. In the Pacific, Australia's Bureau of Meteorology says average weekly sea temperatures in the Central Ocean are the highest it has on record. A daily mark in the Central Eastern Pacific in September already passed the very strong El Nino of 2015, the BBC reports, and the expected peak is still

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.200
December. Forecasters in Australia and the United States now use a relative index, so

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:40.180
human-caused ocean warming does not hide the natural spike. On that index, the Bureau's

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:44.760
Weekly Series, which starts in 2008, is already above December 2015.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:50.220
Zeke Housefather, a climate scientist at Berkeley Earth, says this year's strength is spilling

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:58.160
past the usual monitoring box. Set beside the big events of 1972, 1982, 1997, and 2015,

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:02.360
The warm water reaches farther across the Pacific and into the Gulf of Mexico.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:07.120
The pattern turns up about every two to seven years, and usually runs for about a year.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:13.860
Ukraine's president Volodymyr Zelensky said his forces stopped hitting Russian oil refineries

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:18.400
for two days after Donald Trump called for an energy ceasefire, and that Moscow did not

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.640
heed the American president.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:25.320
He said Russia used more than 100 weapons overnight, jet-powered drones, loitering munitions

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:30.720
and ballistic missiles, and that 19 regions were hit in those two days, including energy sites,

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:35.620
the Guardian reports. In Carkeev, he said, rescuers worked through the night under a

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:40.820
destroyed apartment building. Four people were killed, 41 were hurt in that city in one evening.

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:46.120
NBC News reported that Trump told reporters the two sides agreed because he told them to agree,

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:52.500
and that he knew neither had signed on when he announced the pause. Former Congolese President

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:57.400
Joseph Kabila has been named head of a new rebel coalition, the front for the re-foundation of

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:01.900
the nation. The group says it will line up resistance forces to end what it calls tyranny,

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:07.760
and that it will use every means, including force, the BBC reports. Advisor Claude Ibelanki

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:12.040
made the announcement Monday at Kabila's house in Goma, the biggest city in the east,

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:16.900
which the M23 has held since last year. Video from the group shows Kabila signing.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:22.660
M-23 leader Sultani Makenga is one of four deputies. The other three also come from the

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:29.860
AFC M-23 alliance that took much of the mineral-rich east. Kabila is 55. He governed from 2001 until

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:36.140
January 2019, had denied ties to the M-23 and was sentenced to death in absentia for trees in a

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:41.280
year ago. The Congolese government has not commented. The naming is the clearest public sign yet

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:46.560
of a direct armed role against President Felix Toshiketti. French supermarket chain said Monday

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:51.240
that a cyber-attack pushed fridge temperatures up in hundreds of stores and left spoiled food

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:51.760
to be dumped.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.280
France 24 reported fires as well.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:59.400
The New York Times says the hit was on a Danish software system in at least 380 shops,

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.520
some of which throughout Frozen Goods.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.440
The attackers have not been identified.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:07.060
Cold storage failed at once for customers and staff in those stores.

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:14.160
Two small airports in Ohio, Youngstown Warren and Akron Canton are a main cog in the Trump

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:18.700
administration's Great Lakes deportation flights, the Guardian reports. Youngstown

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:24.740
Warren has no commercial service. Last year it logged 398 contracted shuffle and removal flights.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:31.240
An advocacy tally, ICE flights monitor counts about 300 flights so far this year from each airport.

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:35.740
Only seven other American airports have more of those shuffle flights than the pair combined.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:41.120
The planes on the ground can take about 300 people at a time and each day a contracted network

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:45.680
moves hundreds of immigrants among Wisconsin, Michigan, Ohio, and Massachusetts.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:51.160
France's Senate is due to take up a bill the National Assembly passed in July

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:56.260
that would treat police gunfire on duty as self-defense unless a complainant proves otherwise,

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:02.700
Al Jazeera reports. Foreign ministers from 32 countries, in a statement carried by Kurdistan 24,

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:08.160
condemned what they described as Iranian proxy attacks, and backed Britain's account of a 27th

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.460
of September incident at RAF Fairford.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:16.680
In Western Mexico, CBC says Hurricane Simon killed one person in Guerrero, and post-tropical

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:20.580
cyclone Rachel killed four in Baja, California, with others still missing.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.760
South Korea's president Lee Jae-myeong told his cabinet the American Alliance is the main

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:30.580
axis of diplomacy, and that a cow-towing line should be refused, while U.S. intelligence

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.860
sharing stays limited, YonHap reports.

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:37.760
reports. Early voting opened Tuesday in Georgia for one U.S. Senate seat and every state

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:42.220
white office, with the White House and the Republican Party watching closely, democracy

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:48.160
docket reports. Brazil's Senate is where the case on both sides of the six-day work week

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:53.080
now sits. A constitutional amendment would swap six days on and one off for five days

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:58.500
on and two off. Senate President Davi Alcalumbre has said debates today and Wednesday can lead

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.940
into a first-round vote, and it is the only item on the floor this week. President

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:06.740
Lieutenant Louise Inacio Lula de Silva's government once both rounds done before the

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.900
campaign ends on the 25th of October.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:13.740
Government leader Teresa Laitao is expected by Wednesday to ask for a special calendar

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:15.440
that shortens the gap between rounds.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:19.980
The rulebook wants five discussion sessions before the first vote, and three already

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:20.880
happened last week.

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:25.540
A yes vote then needs five business days and three more sessions before a second round.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:30.300
O'Globo describes the amendment as Lula's campaign banner, and the government's push

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.060
is to lock in that extra rest day before the 25th.

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:36.740
Flavio Bolsonaro argues the other way.

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:39.300
He wants workers to bargain hours with employers.

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:43.080
The same idea from campaign coordinator Senator Rogerio Moreno,

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:45.360
who would rather the liberal party abstain.

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:48.360
Senate party leader Carlos Portino called the bill

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:50.920
an out-of-control electoral vehicle supposedly

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:52.600
steered by Alcalumbre in Lula.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:55.300
Senator Wellington Fagundez said the campaign

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:58.500
prefers abstention, but most of the bench wants a clear vote.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:03.720
Senator Teresa Christina said other opposition parties should free their members, too, at a lunch

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:04.260
on Wednesday.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.980
None of those accounts says which way the vote will go.

